  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and Rationale\n\nThe proposed strategy focuses on iterative constrained optimization with adaptive sampling and a fallback mechanism. Central idea: exploit the step function structure and use gradient-based optimization with careful perturbation to escape local minima, incorporating a low-resolution auxiliary function to guide high-resolution steps.\n\n**Rationale**:\n- Direct gradient descent may converge to suboptimal local minima due to the highly nonconvex overlap function.\n- Multi-resolution approach leverages coarser approximations to explore diverse solutions while refining at higher resolutions.\n- Perturbative steps with memory help escape local minima while preserving key structural features.\n- Fallback ensures valid solutions even if optimization stalls.\n\n**Limitations**:\n- Requires careful balancing between exploration and exploitation.\n- Memory of prior solutions requires additional computation.",
